cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying datasets, please cite them as below."
title: "Finite radial prolate framework: computational pipeline and CPSWF benchmark datasets"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python pipeline for the finite radial prolate framework: assembling the finite
  radial prolate matrix on a Bessel-zero grid as the operator image of the continuous principal
  operator B_R B_K B_R, solving its eigenproblem, and reconstructing continuous approximants of
  the circular/radial prolate spheroidal wave functions (CPSWFs), together with the ground-truth
  benchmark, validation-campaign, and pilot datasets. This archive is the computational
  companion to the manuscript "Fourier-Bessel Ritz Approximation of Circular Prolate Spheroidal
  Wave Functions" by Natalie Baddour.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baddour
    given-names: Natalie
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7025-7501"
    affiliation: "Department of Mechanical Engineering, University of Ottawa, Ottawa, Ontario, Canada"
    email: "nbaddour@uottawa.ca"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - prolate spheroidal wave functions
  - circular prolate spheroidal wave functions
  - Hankel transform
  - Slepian concentration
  - Fourier-Bessel
  - discrete prolate spheroidal sequences
  - spectral concentration
